      "comment": "While it is technically true that the U.S. government funds Viagra, and other erectile dysfunction medications — in fact, the $41.6 million figure cited on the sign is significantly lower than the total amount of taxpayer funds spent on ED medications — the government funding comes entirely through the Department of Defense, and is spent as part of the Defense Health Agency (DHA) budget to purchase Viagra and other popular medications for erectile dysfunction for retired military veterans, as well as active-duty service members, according to a report on the Viagra funding by the Military Times. The DHA also covers birth control medications and treatments for active and retired service members, according to listings on the website for Tricare, the managed health care service for members of the military and veterans. -Inquisitr",
